      "criterion": "task",
      "subSkill": "specific-detail",
      "advice": "For the project answer, explain what you did in the workshops, what compromise emerged and what changed as a result. Those details would show your own contribution rather than just naming the activity.",
      "evidence": "The answer ends at “j'ai organisé des ateliers pour trouver un compromis”, without saying what the compromise was or whether it worked."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "task",
      "subSkill": "inference",
      "advice": "When asked to reconsider a project under a constraint, explain the trade-off behind your decision and its likely consequence. Practise giving a reason after each proposed change.",
      "evidence": "The typed response says “j'aurais priorisé les régions avec le plus de demandes et reporté le reste à l'année suivante”, but gives no reason for that priority or discussion of the effect of postponement."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "grammar",
      "subSkill": "agreement",
      "advice": "In spoken practice, check the subject before using a verb with a plural noun. Repeat short project descriptions with plural subjects until the verb ending is reliable.",
      "evidence": "The spoken answers contain “les dossiers devient” and “les régions voulait”."
    }
  ],
  "missingWords": [
